  [1mRunner:[0m Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode --test[39m. It ships with Node, reads [38;5;153m.mjs[39m natively, and adds zero dependencies — which is
  why the [38;5;153m.mjs[39m choice in Approach A pays off here. [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m gains one line: [38;5;153m"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }[39m.

  [1mThe one design constraint testing imposes:[0m Node has no [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m, so [38;5;153msession.mjs[39m must read
  [38;5;153mglobalThis.sessionStorage[39m [3mat call time[0m, not capture it at module load. If it grabbed the reference on import, tests
  could never swap in a fake. Worth writing down, because it's the kind of detail an implementer "tidies" into a
  module-level const and quietly breaks every test.

  The fake is a Map-backed [38;5;153mgetItem[39m/[38;5;153msetItem[39m/[38;5;153mremoveItem[39m, plus a throwing variant for the storage-unavailable path.

